{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Take heed regarding the plague of tzara'at</b>. This too is an explicit commandment, adding a negative prohibition concerning one who cuts off his bright spot, or likewise concerning one who refrains from showing his plague to the priest. But concerning the laws of plagues themselves, he did not mention them here; rather, he warned here only: according to all that they instruct you, the Levitical priests, as I have commanded them — because the priests are zealous and it is sufficient for them with what He commanded them, as I have already explained (at the beginning of the book)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:54:42.429039323Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}